<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thomas-Robert Bugeaud</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1784">1784</a>–<a href="/years/1849">1849</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thomas-Robert Bugeaud (1784–1849) was a French marshal who, as governor-general of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a> from 1840 to 1847, led the conquest of the country against Abd al-Qadir. He used mobile columns and a scorched-earth policy of raids, defeated the Moroccan army at Isly in 1844 and encouraged European settlement. He died of cholera in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> in 1849.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thomas-robert-bugeaud.jpg" alt="Thomas-Robert Bugeaud" width="320" height="496" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles-Philippe Larivière · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bugeaud,_Thomas_-_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
